  "answer": "To reduce the risk of credit assignment failure caused by delayed rewards, it has been proposed to integrate RUDDER reward redistribution during reinforcement learning fine-tuning (https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.07857). This intervention replaces the original delayed rewards with redistributed rewards so that the expected future reward per step is near zero, leading to faster and lower-variance learning (https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.07857). The proposed implementation mechanisms for this include second-order Markov reward redistribution, which uses differences of consecutive Q-values (https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.07857), and LSTM-based return prediction with contribution analysis, which uses an LSTM to predict the episode-wide return at every time step and assigns redistributed rewards via the differences of consecutive predictions (https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.07857)."
